			"text": "Taemasosteus is a genus of buchanosteid placoderm known from the Emsian aged Taemas-Weejasper Reef and Buchan Group in Australia. Taemasosteus is known from large isolated plates, revealing a large animal, about a meter in length. It shares some similarities to members of the closely related Homostiidae, and is therefore thought to be a basal member of Buchanosteidae."
